IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, sections 107.1 to 111.1 and 118 -- THE ACCOUNTS OF CANADA.
-- Piece cp6, lines 2779 to 2849 and 3086 to 3099 of the Act file.
--
-- Section 107.1 lets the Minister accept gifts and bequests and binds the Minister to their terms. Section 108 establishes the
-- Canada Pension Plan Account (the base plan), lists what is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to it and what is
-- charged to it, and caps what may be paid out. Section 108.1 moves surplus to the Investment Board and lets the Minister call it back,
-- and has the Minister of Finance credit interest. Sections 108.2 and 108.3 do the same for the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account.
-- Section 110 charges interest on a shortfall. Section 111.1 lets the Minister of Finance agree with the Investment Board. Section 118
-- makes the Crown pay, as employer, what Part I makes an employer pay, into the right account.
--
-- THESE PROVISIONS ADDRESS OFFICIALS AND ACCOUNTS. They are encoded for what they decide (which account a contribution of a tier goes
-- to; whether an amount is a credit or a charge; how much may be paid out; on what amount and for what days interest runs) and the
-- seat does not ask them: a contributor cannot state the balance of an account of Canada. See NOTES.md, seat.
-- Sections 108(1) and 108.2(1) ("There is hereby established ... an account to be known as ...") are encoded as the
-- enumeration Account of Canada: it is the only thing they decide.
--
-- Sorting a contribution into the base plan or the additional plan uses the core's Tier: section 108(2)(a) credits contributions under
-- subsections 8(1), 9(1) and 10(1) to the Canada Pension Plan Account and section 108.2(2)(a) credits those under (1.1) and (1.2) to the
-- Additional Canada Pension Plan Account; the core's rule names the subsection of each tier.
--
-- THE JURAL RELATIONS: the donor's power to bind the Minister to terms (s 107.1); the Minister of Finance's duties to credit and charge
-- (ss 108.1(3), 108.3(3), 110) with no holder of the claim named; the Minister's power to require the Investment Board to pay, and the
-- Board's liability (ss 108.1(2), 108.3(2)); the Crown's duty, as employer, to pay into the right account (s 118).
-- Money is a NUMBER of Canadian dollars; a rate is a fraction.

§ `Part III -- the accounts of Canada (sections 107.1 to 111.1 and 118)`

§§ `Section 107.1 -- donations`

-- src:2780 | Donations
-- src:2781 | 107.1 The Minister may acquire money, securities or other property by gift, bequest or otherwise and shall dispose of such securities or other property subject to the terms, if any, on which such money, securities or other property is given, bequeathed or otherwise made available to the Minister.
@ref Act s 107.1 (src:2780-2781)
GIVEN `the money, securities or other property is made available to the Minister by gift, bequest or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 107.1 — the Minister may acquire the money, securities or other property` `the money, securities or other property is made available to the Minister by gift, bequest or otherwise` MEANS
    `the money, securities or other property is made available to the Minister by gift, bequest or otherwise`

-- "shall dispose of such securities or other property subject to the terms, if any, on which [they are] given": the Minister
-- is bound only where there are terms, and only in disposing of securities or other property (not money).
@ref Act s 107.1 (src:2780-2781)
GIVEN `the property is securities or other property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `terms were stated on which the property was made available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 107.1 — the Minister must dispose of the property subject to the terms on which it was made available` `the property is securities or other property` `terms were stated on which the property was made available` MEANS
    `the property is securities or other property` AND `terms were stated on which the property was made available`

§§ `Sections 108 and 108.2 -- the two accounts, and what is credited to them`

-- Sections 108(1) and 108.2(1): the two accounts established in the accounts of Canada.
-- src:2782 | Canada Pension Plan Account
-- src:2783 | 108 (1) There is hereby established in the accounts of Canada an account to be known as the Canada Pension Plan Account.
-- src:2812 | Additional Canada Pension Plan Account
-- src:2813 | 108.2 (1) There is established in the accounts of Canada an account to be known as the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account.
@ref Act s 108(1) (src:2782-2783), s 108.2(1) (src:2812-2813)
DECLARE `cp6 Account of Canada under the Act` IS ONE OF
    `the Canada Pension Plan Account`
    `the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account`

-- "all amounts received under this Act as or on account of contributions under subsections 8(1), 9(1) and 10(1)" go to the
-- Canada Pension Plan Account; those "under subsections 8(1.1) and (1.2), 9(1.1) and (1.2) and 10(1.1) and (1.2)" go to the
-- Additional Canada Pension Plan Account. The core's Tier is the sorting of the six subsections into three tiers.
@ref Act s 108(2)(a) (src:2786), s 108.2(2)(a) (src:2816)
GIVEN tier IS A Tier
GIVETH A `cp6 Account of Canada under the Act`
`s 108(2)(a) and 108.2(2)(a) — the account to which a contribution of a tier is credited` tier MEANS
    CONSIDER tier
    WHEN `the base tier` THEN `the Canada Pension Plan Account`
    WHEN `the first additional tier` THEN `the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account`
    WHEN `the second additional tier` THEN `the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account`

-- src:2784 | Amounts to be credited to Account
-- src:2785 | (2) There shall be paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account
-- src:2786 | (a) all amounts received under this Act as or on account of contributions under subsections 8(1), 9(1) and 10(1) or otherwise on account of the base Canada Pension Plan;
-- src:2787 | (b) all amounts required to be credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account pursuant to any agreement entered into under subsection 39(1) or 80(1) or pursuant to any regulation made under paragraph 89(1)(j) or subsection 107(3);
-- src:2788 | (c) [Repealed, 2016, c. 14, s. 44]
-- src:2789 | (d) any amount of money received under section 107.1 on account of the base Canada Pension Plan and any proceeds from the disposition of any securities or other property received under that section on account of the base Canada Pension Plan;
-- src:2790 | (e) all amounts charged for the use of resources that are associated with the administration of this Act in relation to the base Canada Pension Plan;
-- src:2791 | (f) any interest or administrative charge collected in relation to money payable under this Act in relation to the base Canada Pension Plan; and
-- src:2792 | (g) all amounts received under subsection 56(1) of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act.
-- src:2793 | (2.1) [Repealed, 2012, c. 19, s. 234]
-- out of range: sections 8, 9 and 10 (piece cp1); section 39 (piece cp2); sections 80 and 89 (piece cp5); section 56 and 57 of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act (another Act, not deposited).
-- The members name the provisions that supply each kind of amount; this module does not read them.
DECLARE `cp6 Kind of amount that may be credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account` IS ONE OF
    `a contribution under subsection 8(1), 9(1) or 10(1), or another amount received on account of the base Canada Pension Plan`
    `an amount required to be credited to the Account under an agreement under subsection 39(1) or 80(1) or a regulation under paragraph 89(1)(j) or subsection 107(3)`
    `money received under section 107.1 on account of the base Canada Pension Plan, or the proceeds of disposing of securities or property so received`
    `an amount charged for the use of resources associated with the administration of the Act in relation to the base Canada Pension Plan`
    `interest or an administrative charge collected in relation to money payable under the Act in relation to the base Canada Pension Plan`
    `an amount received under subsection 56(1) of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act`
    `any other amount`

@ref Act s 108(2) (src:2784-2793)
GIVEN kind IS A `cp6 Kind of amount that may be credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 108(2) — the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `any other amount` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
    -- Paragraph (c) and subsection (2.1) are repealed in this text and state nothing.

