§§ `Section 110 -- interest on a shortfall`

-- Interest is charged "on any amount paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under subsection 108(3) that exceeds the balance
-- to the credit of the Canada Pension Plan Account": the amount over the balance, and nothing when it does not exceed it.
-- The rate ("market rates, as determined by that Minister") is the Minister of Finance's and is not computed here.
-- src:2841 | Interest — Canada Pension Plan Account
-- src:2842 | 110 (1) The Minister of Finance shall charge interest to the Canada Pension Plan Account at market rates, as determined by that Minister, on any amount paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under subsection 108(3) that exceeds the balance to the credit of the Canada Pension Plan Account. Interest is to be charged for the period beginning on the day on which the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under subsection 108(3) and ending on the day on which the Investment Board pays that amount into the Consolidated Revenue Fund under subsection 56(1) of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act.
@ref Act s 110(1) (src:2841-2842)
GIVEN `the amount paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under subsection 108(3)` IS A NUMBER
      `the balance to the credit of the Canada Pension Plan Account` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 110(1) — the amount on which interest is charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `the amount paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under subsection 108(3)` `the balance to the credit of the Canada Pension Plan Account` MEANS
    max 0 ((`the amount paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under subsection 108(3)`) MINUS (`the balance to the credit of the Canada Pension Plan Account`))

-- "for the period beginning on the day on which the amount is paid out ... and ending on the day on which the Investment Board
-- pays that amount into the Consolidated Revenue Fund under subsection 56(1) of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act":
-- both days are in the period; how the period is counted into an amount of interest is not stated.
@ref Act s 110(1) (src:2841-2842)
GIVEN `the day the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund` IS A DATE
      `the day the Investment Board pays the amount into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 110(1) — a day is in the period for which interest is charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `the day the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `the day the Investment Board pays the amount into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` day MEANS
    day AT LEAST `the day the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund` AND day AT MOST `the day the Investment Board pays the amount into the Consolidated Revenue Fund`

-- src:2843 | Interest — Additional Canada Pension Plan Account
-- src:2844 | (2) The Minister of Finance shall charge interest to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account at market rates, as determined by that Minister, on any amount paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under subsection 108.2(3) that exceeds the balance to the credit of the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account. Interest is to be charged for the period beginning on the day on which the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under subsection 108.2(3) and ending on the day on which the Investment Board pays that amount into the Consolidated Revenue Fund under subsection 56(1.1) of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act.
@ref Act s 110(2) (src:2843-2844)
GIVEN `the amount paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under subsection 108.2(3)` IS A NUMBER
      `the balance to the credit of the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 110(2) — the amount on which interest is charged to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `the amount paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under subsection 108.2(3)` `the balance to the credit of the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` MEANS
    max 0 ((`the amount paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under subsection 108.2(3)`) MINUS (`the balance to the credit of the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account`))

@ref Act s 110(2) (src:2843-2844)
GIVEN `the day the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund` IS A DATE
      `the day the Investment Board pays the amount into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 110(2) — a day is in the period for which interest is charged to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `the day the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `the day the Investment Board pays the amount into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` day MEANS
    day AT LEAST `the day the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund` AND day AT MOST `the day the Investment Board pays the amount into the Consolidated Revenue Fund`

§§ `Section 111.1 -- administration agreements with the Investment Board`

-- src:2846 | Administration agreement
-- src:2847 | 111.1 (1) The Minister of Finance may, on terms and conditions satisfactory to the Minister, enter into an agreement with the Investment Board with respect to the administration of any matter referred to in sections 107.1 to 110, including the payment of amounts out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund to the Investment Board, and the payment of amounts by the Investment Board into the Consolidated Revenue Fund.
@ref Act s 111.1(1) (src:2846-2847)
GIVEN `the matter is one referred to in sections 107.1 to 110, including payments to and from the Investment Board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms and conditions are satisfactory to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 111.1(1) — the Minister of Finance may enter into an agreement with the Investment Board about the matter` `the matter is one referred to in sections 107.1 to 110, including payments to and from the Investment Board` `the terms and conditions are satisfactory to the Minister` MEANS
    `the matter is one referred to in sections 107.1 to 110, including payments to and from the Investment Board` AND `the terms and conditions are satisfactory to the Minister`

-- src:2848 | Administration agreement
-- src:2849 | (2) The Minister of Finance may enter into an agreement with the Investment Board with respect to the administration of any matter referred to in section 113.
@ref Act s 111.1(2) (src:2848-2849)
GIVEN `the matter is one referred to in section 113` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 111.1(2) — the Minister of Finance may enter into an agreement with the Investment Board about the matter` `the matter is one referred to in section 113` MEANS
    `the matter is one referred to in section 113`

§§ `Section 118 -- government contributions as employer`

-- Out of range: the contributions required to be made by Her Majesty under subsections 9(1), (1.1) and (1.2) (piece cp1) and the
-- amounts required by subsection 21(2) (piece cp2) are plain inputs, in dollars.
-- src:3086 | Government Employees
-- src:3087 | Government contributions — Canada Pension Plan Account
-- src:3088 | 118 (1) There is to be charged to the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account an amount equal to
-- src:3089 | (a) the contributions required to be made by Her Majesty in right of Canada under subsection 9(1) in respect of persons in employment under Her Majesty in right of Canada that is not excepted employment under this Act, and
-- src:3090 | (b) the amount required by subsection 21(2) to be paid by Her Majesty in right of Canada as a result of the failure to deduct and remit, in accordance with this Act, the required amount as or on account of contributions required to be made under subsection 8(1) by persons referred to in paragraph (a).
-- out of range: sections 8(1) and 9(1) (piece cp1); subsection 21(2) (piece cp2). The two amounts are plain inputs; this module does not compute them.
@ref Act s 118(1) (src:3086-3090)
GIVEN `the contributions required to be made by Her Majesty in right of Canada under subsection 9(1) in respect of persons in employment under Her Majesty that is not excepted employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount required by subsection 21(2) to be paid by Her Majesty for failing to deduct and remit the contributions required to be made under subsection 8(1) by those persons` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 118(1) — the amount charged to the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `the contributions required to be made by Her Majesty in right of Canada under subsection 9(1) in respect of persons in employment under Her Majesty that is not excepted employment` `the amount required by subsection 21(2) to be paid by Her Majesty for failing to deduct and remit the contributions required to be made under subsection 8(1) by those persons` MEANS
    (`the contributions required to be made by Her Majesty in right of Canada under subsection 9(1) in respect of persons in employment under Her Majesty that is not excepted employment`)
        PLUS (`the amount required by subsection 21(2) to be paid by Her Majesty for failing to deduct and remit the contributions required to be made under subsection 8(1) by those persons`)

-- src:3091 | Government contributions — Additional Canada Pension Plan Account
-- src:3092 | (1.1) There is to be charged to the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account an amount equal to
-- src:3093 | (a) the contributions required to be made by Her Majesty in right of Canada under subsections 9(1.1) and (1.2) in respect of persons in employment under Her Majesty in right of Canada that is not excepted employment under this Act, and
-- src:3094 | (b) the amount required by subsection 21(2) to be paid by Her Majesty in right of Canada as a result of the failure to deduct and remit, in accordance with this Act, the required amount as or on account of contributions required to be made under subsections 8(1.1) and (1.2) by persons referred to in paragraph (a).
-- out of range: sections 8(1) and 9(1) (piece cp1); subsection 21(2) (piece cp2). The two amounts are plain inputs; this module does not compute them.
